<title>LUXEMBOURG: Italian farmers protest about EU farm policies.</title>
<headline>Italian farmers protest about EU farm policies.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>By plane, train and coach some 7,000 Italian farmers on Monday converged on a meeting of European Union farm ministers to peacefully protest against EU farm policies.</p>
<p>With Luciano Pavarotti urging them on to victory in a dramatic recording of the Tosca aria &quot;Nessun dorma,&quot; they stood in brilliant sunshine before a giant banner proclaiming &quot;Don't let Europe betray Italian Agriculture.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;Farm prices are falling and farmers' revenues are declining. We want a fairer deal,&quot; railed Paolo Micolini, president of the Coldiretti farmers' union, one of Italy's largest.</p>
<p>Wearing yellow caps, waving yellow flags and flying multi-coloured balloons, the farmers demanded higher milk production quotas and a bigger share of EU subsidies for wine, olive oil and other Mediterranean farm products.</p>
</text>
